Z||000001||My7Fieros||05-03-2001||02:27 AM||||It looks similar to that. Its basically a color changing paint. For example, at one angle it may look green, another it may look purple, and yet another angle it may look bronze.<BR>Its a house of colors paint...prepair yourself, I actually priced it once and it can run up 600 bucks a quart! (Granted, one quart will paint a Fiero, due to the fact that after you mix it w/ reducer and what-not, it turns out to be two quarts sprayable).<BR>None the less, it ain't cheap! This was through Colormatch...a local automotive paint store that specializes in Dupont and House of Color paints here in Memphis. M7F<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||4
